    <summary>A fast, native desktop GUI for browsing and querying large JSON files with jq, JSONPath, JMESPath and JSON Pointer.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
**jsonquery gui** is a native desktop tool for browsing and querying large JSON files. Drag in a file, open a URL or paste JSON directly, then query it with jq, JSON Pointer (RFC 6901), JSONPath (RFC 9535) or JMESPath. Results stream into a searchable tree or text view.

## Features

- Four query dialects: jq, JSON Pointer, JSONPath and JMESPath
- Handles large files: results stream in instead of freezing the window
- Optional inline autocomplete for each dialect's functions and for the loaded document's own keys
- Colour-coded query box and a built-in tutorial with live results for all four dialects
- Built in Rust with egui; a single self-contained executable

## Package notes

- The package downloads the official release zip from GitHub and checks its SHA-256 before extracting it.
- It adds a **jsonquery gui** Start-menu shortcut and a `jsonquery-gui` command (`jsonquery-gui file.json`).
- The executable is not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen may warn the first time it runs.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/nujufas/jsonquery_gui/releases/tag/v0.4.1</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
